  "body": "## What changed\n\nSet `lead_arc_radius: None` in the model arc test fixture. No application code or test assertions change.\n\nThe merge of #4002 adds the required field to `WireContourOp`. The fixture from #3215 did not initialize it. `None` keeps the original straight lead. The decision is in `docs/decisions/4061-wire-test-build.md`.\n\n## Evidence and checks\n\nBase: `83d52ef6a283497e00a1a13c8403ee4671cd7795`.\n\n- The existing artifact from run [45684660319](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/45684660319) reports E0063 at `crates/app/tests/wire_post/model_arcs.rs:42`.\n- Before the fix, `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_post --no-run -j 3` fails with the same E0063.\n- After the fix, `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wire_post -j 3 -- --test-threads=1` passes all 22 tests. This includes all four `model_arcs::` tests and the existing golden and refusal checks.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` passes. The actual selected step runs all four `model_arcs::` tests; it is not a dry-run or an empty plan.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test wire_post -j 3 -- -D warnings` passes.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n\nThe checks use the existing Linux environment with a three-job limit. This is a mechanical test compilation repair. The existing target fails before the fix; no additional regression test is needed.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe full app test build, batch gate, light lane, heavy lanes, example catalog, GUI, and physical controls were not run. No hosted workflow was restarted. The reported hosted batch failure is not a green hosted result.\n\nCurrent AGENTS asks for the release-mode light lane at review. The owner's authorized scope prohibits release rebuilds for this fixture-only repair. This conflict is disclosed rather than reporting an unrun lane as passed.\n\nNo generation, post, geometry, simulation, collision, or output safety rule changes. No claim of physical-machine safety.\n\n## Contribution trace\n\nClaim: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4061#issuecomment-7172719183\n\nGitHub refused the claim label update. The public claim comment is the fallback; no label or assignment was set. No duplicate fix was found. Coder used bounded exact-error source inspection without a scout under the owner's single-worker scope.\n\nThis PR does not close the automated gate issue by hand. The next green post-merge run closes it.\n\nChangelog: none (test fixture compilation only).\n\nEffort: low. No escalation.\n\nRefs #4061\n",
